# Keep the build context small, and keep secrets out of it entirely.
.git
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage

# Never ship env files into the image: the builder skips validation and the runtime
# gets its env injected, so a stray .env in the context is pure leak risk.
.env*
!.env.example

*.pem
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

.firebase/
*-debug.log

# Playwright per-run artifacts. Excluded for the same reason `.env*` and `*.pem`
# are, not merely to keep the context small: `trace: 'retain-on-failure'` records
# the network log of a real sign-in — the session cookie and the seed password —
# and `screenshot: 'only-on-failure'` writes a picture of the authenticated UI.
# `Containerfile`'s `COPY . .` would bake those into the BUILDER layer, which the
# shipped image does not carry but the local build cache does, and which travels
# with any `--cache-to` export or `--target builder` push.
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

docs
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Local emulator data and the Python services are not part of the dashboard image.
.emulator-data
firebase-export-*
services
